// #189 — the committed integration pin for a PRODUCER stage's constructed candidate.
//
// ⭐ BOTH VALUE MODES: `BMI` is a Quantity FORMULA over two operands (so its §5b stamp is a `Max`), `Obese`
// is a boolean THRESHOLD over one (so its stamp is that operand's). Both are `code is` + a `definition is`
// pipeline + a `coded from` posrep — the goal's shape.
//
// ⚠ THE DECISION DELIBERATELY GUARDS ON A NON-PRODUCER CONCEPT. A member-existence interface over a
// producer-bearing referent is REFUSED (`lowerLocalCodes`): its arms read the retrieves directly, so it would
// publish `false` while the referent's merge publishes the computed value. The emitter applies NO
// reachability filtering, so `BMI` and `Obese` still emit in full — which is what this fixture pins.
